==English==
{{was wotd|2017|March|10}}
[[File:Raphanus sativus.jpg|thumb|A bowl of radishes (''[[Raphanus sativus]]'' or [[Raphanus raphanistrum subsp. sativus|''Raphanus raphanistrum'' subsp. ''sativus'']] ''(sense 2)''. Such radishes have a [[pungent]] taste and are usually eaten [[raw]] in [[salads]], etc.]]
[[File:2010-06-18-supermarkt-by-RalfR-5.jpg|thumb|The [[daikon]], a [[cultivar]] or [[subspecies]] of radish. It has a [[mild]] taste and is generally [[cook#Verb|cooked]] before eating.]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alter|en|raddish||obsolete}}

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|radiche}}, from {{inh|en|ang|rǣdiċ}}, from {{inh|en|gmw-pro|*rādik}}, borrowed from {{der|en|la|radix|rādīcem|t=[[root]] of a [[plant]]; radish}}; later influenced by {{der|en|xno|radich}} and {{der|en|frm|radice}}, borrowed from {{der|en|it|radice}}, from the same Latin source.

